Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedseq.shoddy — reckoner seed: list and pair structure
Rem
Rem RANGE, LENGTH, REVERSE, CONCAT, FIRST, REST and SORTL work a LIST
Rem cell; PAIR, HEAD and TAIL work a PAIR cell — "rate" 0.05 PAIR gives
Rem records on the stack, per R2.8's note on Pair bridging. Most of
Rem these are one line over a builtin the language already has (Range,
Rem Length, Reverse, Concat, Sort); the seed's job is only to fence off
Rem the cases those builtins Error on.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- RANGE ------------------------------------------------------------

Def SqSeedRange(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RANGE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqRange(vs)), "( a b -- list )", "The whole numbers from a up to b, one cell per value; empty when b is below a.")

Def SqRange(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("RANGE", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(a)
            SqRangeTo(a, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RANGE did not answer")

Def SqRangeTo(a As Number, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("RANGE", c)
        Case Ok(b)
            RckVals({ CutList(Map(Range(a, b), CutNum)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RANGE did not answer")

Rem ---- LENGTH, REVERSE -----------------------------------------------------
Rem Both total over any list, empty included.

Def SqSeedLength(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "LENGTH", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqLength(vs)), "( list -- n )", "How many elements a list holds.")

Def SqLength(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("LENGTH", First(vs))
        Case Ok(xs)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Length(xs)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("LENGTH did not answer")

Def SqSeedReverse(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "REVERSE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqReverse(vs)), "( list -- list )", "The list back to front.")

Def SqReverse(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("REVERSE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(xs)
            RckVals({ CutList(Reverse(xs)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("REVERSE did not answer")

Rem ---- CONCAT ---------------------------------------------------------

Def SqSeedConcat(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "CONCAT", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqConcat(vs)), "( xs ys -- list )", "Two lists joined end to end.")

Def SqConcat(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("CONCAT", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SqConcatY(xs, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("CONCAT did not answer")

Def SqConcatY(xs As List Of Cell, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("CONCAT", c)
        Case Ok(ys)
            RckVals({ CutList(Concat(xs, ys)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("CONCAT did not answer")

Rem ---- FIRST, REST ----------------------------------------------------
Rem Both abort on an empty list at the builtin, so both refuse first.

Def SqSeedFirst(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "FIRST", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqFirst(vs)), "( list -- x )", "The first element of a list.")

Def SqFirst(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("FIRST", First(vs))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SqFirstOf(xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("FIRST did not answer")

Def SqFirstOf(xs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        RckWorkBad("FIRST needs a non-empty list")
    Else
        RckVals({ First(xs) })

Def SqSeedRest(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "REST", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqRest(vs)), "( list -- list )", "The list without its first element.")

Def SqRest(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("REST", First(vs))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SqRestOf(xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("REST did not answer")

Def SqRestOf(xs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        RckWorkBad("REST needs a non-empty list")
    Else
        RckVals({ CutList(Rest(xs)) })

Rem ---- SORTL ------------------------------------------------------------
Rem A Cell is a record, so the SORT builtin (which wants raw NUMBERs or
Rem STRINGs) cannot see through one; SORTL unwraps a homogeneous list of
Rem one kind, sorts the raw values, and wraps the answer back up. A list
Rem of anything else — mixed, or a kind that has no order — is refused
Rem by name rather than reaching SORT to be Errored on.

Def SqSeedSortl(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "SORTL", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqSortl(vs)), "( list -- list )", "A list of numbers or a list of strings, sorted ascending.")

Def SqSortl(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("SORTL", First(vs))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SqSortlOf(xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SORTL did not answer")

Def SqSortlOf(xs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        RckVals({ CutList({ }) })
    Else
        SqSortlKind(xs, First(xs))

Def SqSortlKind(xs As List Of Cell, first As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case first
        Case CutNum(x)
            SqSortlNums(xs)
        Case CutStr(t)
            SqSortlStrs(xs)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SORTL needs a list of NUMBERs or a list of STRINGs, got " & CutKindOf(first))

Def SqSortlNums(xs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    If All(xs, SqIsNum) Then
        RckVals({ CutList(Map(Sort(Map(xs, SqNumOf)), CutNum)) })
    Else
        RckWorkBad("SORTL needs every element to be the same kind")

Def SqIsNum(c As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def SqNumOf(c As Cell) As Number
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            x
        Case Else
            0

Def SqSortlStrs(xs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    If All(xs, SqIsStr) Then
        RckVals({ CutList(Map(Sort(Map(xs, SqStrOf)), CutStr)) })
    Else
        RckWorkBad("SORTL needs every element to be the same kind")

Def SqIsStr(c As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(t)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def SqStrOf(c As Cell) As String
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(t)
            t
        Case Else
            ""

Rem ---- PAIR, HEAD, TAIL -------------------------------------------------
Rem Records on the stack: PAIR builds one from any two cells, and HEAD
Rem and TAIL project it back apart. Total — a PAIR cell always has both.

Def SqSeedPair(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "PAIR", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutPair(Pair(Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2))) })), "( a b -- pair )", "Two cells joined as one record.")

Def SqSeedHead(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "HEAD", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqHead(vs)), "( pair -- a )", "The first cell of a pair.")

Def SqHead(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case First(vs)
        Case CutPair(p)
            RckVals({ Fst(p) })
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(RckKindWhy("HEAD", "a PAIR", First(vs)))

Def SqSeedTail(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "TAIL", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SqTail(vs)), "( pair -- b )", "The second cell of a pair.")

Def SqTail(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case First(vs)
        Case CutPair(p)
            RckVals({ Snd(p) })
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(RckKindWhy("TAIL", "a PAIR", First(vs)))

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedSeq(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let st1 = SqSeedRange(RckSeeding(st, "seed-seq"))
    Let st2 = SqSeedLength(st1)
    Let st3 = SqSeedReverse(st2)
    Let st4 = SqSeedConcat(st3)
    Let st5 = SqSeedFirst(st4)
    Let st6 = SqSeedRest(st5)
    Let st7 = SqSeedSortl(st6)
    Let st8 = SqSeedPair(st7)
    Let st9 = SqSeedHead(st8)
    SqSeedTail(st9)
